{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/532654-rules-for-spirit-companions","id":532654,"title":"Rules for Spirit Companions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T19:11:39-07:00","id":532654,"title":"Rules for Spirit Companions?","content":"So i seems that here are plenty of talk of spiris joining in on things, etc, even being pack members, loyal allies, etc. But what I can' find, and what seems to be missing from things like this, are rules on how to figure out how that works mechanically.<br /> <br /> The retainer rules are great. For humans. But what if you want to take a spirit as a Retainer? How do you determine what rank of a spirit you can have per dot level? Those things determine Influence, Numina, etc, so it's not just 'ignore their attributes and use the dice rules from Retainer', they have other things as well.<br /> <br /> There's a three dot wolf-blood Tell that gives you a Familiar, sort of, but it also has some kind of rules about damage absorption which makes it more than just a spirit, so in theory you could get a rank one spirit for less than three dots without that.<br /> <br /> So are there official rules for this somewhere? If not... can there be? It seems like this is something that's gonna come up eventually in lots of games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T09:42:23-07:00","id":534505,"title":"","content":"I mean, quick-handing it. Power, Finesse, and Resistance = Dot level.<br /> 1-2 Dots = Rank 1<br /> 3-4 Dots = Rank 2<br /> 5 Dots = Rank 3<br /> <br /> Have 1 Numen and 1 Manifestation per Rank. May want to have a 1-2 dot &quot;buy in merit&quot; to unlock a Spirit Retainer.<br /> <br /> That said, something official would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:44:35-07:00","id":564199,"title":"","content":"I use:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span> Rank 1, 3 Attribute points, 1 Numen.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span> Rank 1, 5 Attribute points, 2 Numina.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span> Rank 1, 7 Attribute points, 2 Numina.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span> Rank 2, 9 Attribute points, 3 Numina.<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022</span> Rank 2, 11 Attribute points, 3 Numina.<br /> <br /> Species Factor / Size can probably be equal to dots in the Merit. This works out pretty well. It can still be a pretty powerful spirit in player hands. Even makes for a good addition to an Uratha pack aside from their Totem (maybe part of their Totem's brood?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T23:10:53-07:00","id":568825,"title":"","content":"I would take the numen up to 4 at the five dot level, but I could see this working nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5309-chancetr","name":"ChanceTR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5309_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T10:14:06-07:00","id":572838,"title":"","content":"That would be because it's what I'm making you use.<br /> <br /> That said, I tend to downgrade player-controlled NPCs. An ephemeral with those stats is more powerful than a normal human Retainer; that said, they aren't as broadly useful as someone who is human and can operate in human society, which is sort of the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:15:27-07:00","id":573150,"title":"","content":"Hi there,<br /> just wanted to point out to<br /> Werewolf the Forsaken - Forsaken Chronicler's Guide - I - To Isolate<br /> Pg.26, spirit supremacy rules.<br /> <br /> hope it helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. there are also rules for personal totem in pg.25 in the same book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/682-fishmalk","user":"fishmalk","date":".  remembered something 06-29-2015, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/682-fishmalk","name":"fishmalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T14:25:32-07:00","id":573178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fishmalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/532654-rules-for-spirit-companions?p=573150#post573150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi there,<br /> just wanted to point out to<br /> Werewolf the Forsaken - Forsaken Chronicler's Guide - I - To Isolate<br /> Pg.26, spirit supremacy rules.<br /> <br /> hope it helps <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> P.S. there are also rules for personal totem in pg.25 in the same book</div> </div> </div> </div>That's First Edition though. Spirits have some different mechanics in Second Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"u